message: "If you use these results or code, please cite them as below."
title: "Erdős Problem #757: no (4,5)-set with Sidon ratio below 4/7 on fewer than 25 points, and the 14-point classification"
abstract: >-
  Computer-assisted results on Erdős Problem #757 (Tao's constant C_5b). Using the
  3-AP hypergraph reduction of Ma and Tang (arXiv 2602.23282) and the Henning–Yeo
  transversal bound, the only shapes that could beat the upper bound 4/7 within 18
  points are (n,h) = (16,9) and (18,10). An exhaustive isomorph-free enumeration of
  linear 3-graphs with a rank-based realisability test shows that no (4,5)-set with
  (n,h) = (16,9) exists, and that every 14-point (4,5)-set with h = 8 has exactly 12
  three-term progressions and one of 9 progression-hypergraph types.
